  "summary": "Routing of the speedometer cable (speedo shaft, upper and lower halves) and tachometer cable (tach drive shaft) from the transmission and distributor through the firewall (dash panel) to the instrument cluster, all models. The tach cable passes through a sealed grommet in the firewall and is held by a brace clip and by the engine wiring harness clip; the speedo cable passes through a second grommet and is clipped and riveted along the way. At the transmission the speedo cable nut threads onto a fitting, seal and driven gear, held in by a retainer and screw.",
